''The supplied evidence does not identify a cause or justify a code cure.'' The failure excerpt is zero bytes, and the supplied [[full log|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/ci-42178118605.log:6889]] reports a `cli-mesh` failure; it contains no `web-tw5` or `shore-writes` test result. The two failure messages and their stacks are therefore unavailable for diagnosis.

* ''MEASURED:'' The new `port:minted` response is emitted only on `port:want` in [[vessel-host.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-web/src/workers/vessel-host.ts:335]]. The page’s [[vessel-port.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-web/src/vessel-port.ts:86]] switch has no case for it, but also has no default that throws. The production source has no sender of `port:want` or `vessel:claim`.
* ''MEASURED:'' The broker sends `vessel:want` only after a `vessel:claim` at [[ceremony-broker.js|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-web/public/ceremony-broker.js:32]]. The ceremony’s service-worker handler ignores messages without its matching `askId` at [[ceremony.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-web/src/ceremony/ceremony.ts:80]].
* ''MEASURED:'' The `connect` refactor retains the existing `receive` and `lost` handlers; its added branch attaches the minted port’s handler at [[vessel-host.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-web/src/workers/vessel-host.ts:338]]. The instruments report still depends on a painted surface frame at [[main.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-web/src/main.ts:526]], then an animation-frame callback at [[main.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-web/src/main.ts:103]].
* ''INFER:'' These findings do not establish that a new message or dropped handler caused either red. The broker’s new asynchronous `matchAll` before routing every message at [[ceremony-broker.js|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt/packages/lararium-web/public/ceremony-broker.js:19]] changes ceremony timing and remains a possible interaction, but the missing failure details do not establish it. Nor can the load-sensitive handoff establish a pre-existing fault by itself.

''Minimal cure and first red: undetermined.'' First obtain the actual `web-tw5` failure output, including the assertion, timeout location, and captured page/worker errors. Then the lead should reproduce the observed failure with a targeted regression that fails before changing its cause; a file list cannot be named responsibly yet. The browser test opens a preview socket, so ''lead runs'' it. No files were written.

